      "description": "Watch PSV Eindhoven vs Shakhtar Donetsk highlights and goals from UEFA Champions League on ReFooty: Football Highlights Hub. Match played on September 10, 2026. PSV Eindhoven and Shakhtar Donetsk faced off in a highly anticipated UEFA Champions League clash, where tactical discipline and individual flashes of brilliance defined the evening. Both sides looked to assert their dominance in a match that promised to be a crucial test of their European ambitions. First Half Tension and Mendoza’s Opener On September 10, 2026, the atmosphere in Eindhoven was charged with expectation. The home side, PSV Eindhoven , attempted to break the deadlock early through set-pieces, with Filip Kostic and Ivan Perisic delivering dangerous corners that the Ukrainian defense managed to repel. The physical nature of the contest was evident when Vinicius Tobias received a yellow card in the 35th minute. Just as the first half seemed destined to end goalless, Shakhtar Donetsk struck. In the 45th minute, Isaque and Oleg Ocheretko combined to set up Gleiker Mendoza , who slotted home with his right foot. A VAR review confirmed the goal, giving the visitors a slender lead at the break. Dest Sparks the Resurgence PSV Eindhoven wasted no time in responding after the interval. In the 48th minute, Sergino Dest leveled the scores with a clinical right-footed finish, following an assist from Armando Obispo and key involvement from Ruben van Bommel . The equalizer shifted the momentum, but the game soon became a stop-start affair characterized by a flurry of disciplinary actions. The referee’s notebook filled up quickly as Gleiker Mendoza , Pedrinho , Valeriy Bondar , and Obispo were all cautioned during a heated period of play. Late Drama and Shared Points As the clock ticked down, both managers turned to their benches. Shakhtar introduced Lassina Traore and Newerton , while PSV brought on Ryan Flamingo to shore up the midfield. The closing stages were marred by further yellow cards, including one for Sergino Dest for dissent and another for Arda Turan . Despite a late free-kick opportunity for Ivan Perisic that sailed wide, neither side could find a winner. The final whistle blew with the score at 1-1 and possession perfectly balanced at 50%, leaving both teams to settle for a hard-earned point."
